A||N||10||squid||4.3L install update (long)||||4||
Z||000000||squid||07-22-2000||04:50 PM||||The engine is together(from '85 astrovan)and with a short waterpump(4.3's come with long pumps) measures @23" without the 1.5" block adapter. My '85 4spd/3.2L measures 23.5" from the bellhousing to the right frame rail. Archies instructions say to slot the trans mount holes to slide the trans to the left to make more room. I will probably have to "massage" the frame rail, modify my water pump pulley, and use thin headed pulley bolts. Also, a screw-on oil filter bypass with ports that dont come straight out but are parallel to the crank wont fit 4.3's because the filter mounting base is recessed into the block. The corners of the bypass hit the block. They could be cut off but that wouldnt leave any threads for the oil lines. I'm using the "normal type" bypass with 90 degree fittings. I used a P.A.W. $30 alternator bracket which is supposed to mount to the left front on a sbc in the place for an airconditioning compressor on the right frame rail support. In addition, sbc fuel pump block off plates and oil dipsticks and tubes wont interchange. The engine is HEI, 600cfm Holley, .030" over, moly ringed, ported, aluminum roller rockered (1.6), roller timing chained, with the stock '85 tubular manifolds. I have a 4.10 geared 4spd to go with it but I dont know when I will install everything because this Fall(Aug-Dec) is my last semester at school and I am taking 20 hours (big time overload) to finish. ||||reg||4
Z||000001||BizzaroGT||07-24-2000||02:04 AM||||Excellent information!  Keep us posted with your progress, I'm very interested in doing this swap myself.  Post some pictures if you're able to.||||reg||14
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||07-24-2000||02:30 AM||||I will be reading too. I have the complete engine from a 94 S10 but not the information I need to do the swap. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||squid||07-24-2000||07:02 PM||||Since I dont have a digital camera I plan to take some pics this week end, get them developed, scanned, and posted. I need to measure vertically from the cradle to the frame rail. If the center of the water pump shaft is a couple inches above the rail I should be okay since the belt groove is closer to the motor (@21 inches from the bellhousing). Maybe Batboy could tell me if his is above the rail if its belt driven. I also have to order single groove pulleys for a short pump sbc.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||squid||08-08-2000||12:27 PM||||If someone can tell me how to post a picture from my paint file I'll show a couple pics of my 4.3L.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DJRice||08-08-2000||02:44 PM||||To post pictures you need to convert to a <B><I>gif</B></I> or <B><I>jpg</B></I>.  You can do this by downloading an imaging program like Paint Shop Pro and saving each picture in one of the two above mentioned formats.<P>Next, download Pennocks Image Poster, via the blue button at the bottom of this (and most if not all) pages on the forum.  Cliff's PIP page pretty much describes the rest.  Good Luck<P>------------------<BR>Dillon - Titusville, FL<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"Matched Perfect and Staggered Special"||||reg||1
