Z||000008||squid||08-09-2000||10:54 AM||||The pics were sent to me as jpeg but when I try to "save as" my only option is bmp. I checked out Paint Shop Pro but its $100 to down load. Is there a cheap way to save gifs/jpegs just to post/edit size? I havent used my home computer in 2 years(586) because I am REQUIRED to pay $300 per semester(Technology Fee) to have a laptop with internet/email from my college. Its a total rip off. The fees dont even count toward buying it. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||wla21841||10-19-2000||09:20 PM||||If they are already jpeg you don't SAVE AS, Just save the file. <BR>If you bring the picture up on the screen then click the rigt button a window will open up. Pick "save image as".<P>[This message has been edited by wla21841 (edited 10-19-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by wla21841 (edited 10-19-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||mrfiero||10-20-2000||12:19 AM||||Keep us posted squid.....I know I am curious if/how it will all go together (I've been thinking about this swap for many years).<P>One thought though.....you probably want another tranny besides the 4.10.  I have driven a stock V-6 Fiero with a 4.10 and barely had time to shift.  I think with the added power/torque of the 4.3 both first and second gear will probably be useless. <P>Like I said, it's just a thought, but you may want wider gears. ||||reg||10
